#pragma once
static const char piko_lcd_trial_html[] =
"<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\"><title>PIKO LCD Trials</title><style>body{background:#101722;color:#e9eff7;font:16px system-ui}main{max-width:650px;margin:35px auto;padding:20px;background:#1b2636;border-radius:12px}button{display:block;margin:12px 0;padding:13px;border:0;border-radius:8px;background:#256d99;color:white;font:inherit;cursor:pointer}a{color:#70c9ff}small{color:#c0cbd7}</style><main><a href=\"/\">← Home</a><h1>LCD SPI trials</h1><p>Each trial sends red, green and blue stripes. GPIO mapping is experimental; do not use if the device becomes unstable. The backlight is not controlled yet.</p><button onclick=\"trial(1)\">Trial 1 — MOSI23 CLK18 CS5 DC21 RST22, SPI mode 0</button><button onclick=\"trial(2)\">Trial 2 — same GPIOs, SPI mode 3</button><button onclick=\"trial(3)\">Trial 3 — MOSI19 CLK18 CS5 DC21 RST22, SPI mode 0</button><p id=\"result\">Choose one profile. No automatic pin scanning.</p><small>HTTP success means the SPI transfer finished, not that the display showed an image.</small><script>async function trial(n){const e=document.querySelector('#result');e.textContent='Sending profile '+n+'...';try{const r=await fetch('/api/lcd/trial?profile='+n,{method:'POST'});e.textContent='Profile '+n+': HTTP '+r.status+' — '+await r.text()}catch(err){e.textContent='Error: '+err.message}}</script></main></html>\n";
